#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:4
msgid "copyRangeMethod"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:8
msgid ""
"Provides a choice of method for copying data between files. This can be used "
"to optimise copies on network filesystems, improve speed of large copies or "
"clone the data using copy-on-write functionality if the underlying "
"filesystem supports it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:13
msgid "The following values are accepted:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:15
msgid "``standard`` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:16
msgid ""
"Reads the data from source file into application memory, writes the data "
"from application memory into the destination file. (This is the method used "
"by Syncthing prior to this option being introduced.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:20
#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:66
msgid "*Available on: All platforms*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:22
msgid "``copy_file_range``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:23
msgid ""
"Uses the Linux ``copy_file_range`` syscall which, if the underlying "
"filesystem supports it, uses copy-on-write semantics to clone the data. "
"Introduced in Linux 4.5 and tested on XFS and BTRFS. Some network "
"filesystems might use this to perform server-side copies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:28
msgid "*Tested on: BTRFS, EXT4, XFS, ZFS*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:29
#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:42
msgid "*Available on: Linux*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:31
msgid "``ioctl``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:32
msgid ""
"Uses the ``ioctl`` syscall with ``FICLONERANGE`` option which, if the "
"underlying filesystem supports it, uses copy-on-write semantics to clone the "
"data. Officially introduced in Linux 4.5, but was previously known as "
"``BTRFS_IOC_CLONE_RANGE``, which was used to provide copy-on-write semantics "
"to BTRFS filesystems since Linux 2.6.29. Some network filesystems might use "
"this to perform server-side copies. Will fail if not supported by the "
"underlying filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:41
msgid "*Tested on: BTRFS*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:44
msgid "``sendfile``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:45
msgid ""
"Uses the ``sendfile`` syscall which performs in-kernel copy, avoiding having "
"to copy the data into application memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:48
msgid "*Tested on: BTRFS, XFS, EXT4*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:49
msgid "*Available on: Linux, Solaris*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:51
msgid "``duplicate_extents``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:52
msgid ""
"Uses Windows Block Cloning via ``FSCTL_DUPLICATE_EXTENTS_TO_FILE``, which "
"provides copy-on-write semantics to clone the data. Requires Windows 10 "
"v1607 / Windows Server 2016 or later, and a compatible filesystem (ReFS, SMB "
"3.1.1, CsvFS). Will fail if not supported by the underlying filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:58
msgid "*Tested on: ReFS*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:59
msgid "*Available on: Windows*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:61
msgid "``all``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../advanced/folder-copyrangemethod.rst:62
msgid ""
"Tries all of the copy methods in the following order: ``ioctl``, "
"``copy_file_range``, ``sendfile``, ``duplicate_extents``, ``standard``."
msgstr ""
